@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] ziggy-provider-key-custody
Provider keys MUST come from private runtime files. Keys, prompts, responses,
tool payloads and raw upstream errors MUST NOT enter logs or durable accounting.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;deployment] ziggy-underclass-origin
The OpenAI-compatible origin MUST be either the fixed public provider origin
or enrolled host-local Underclass loopback. The latter MUST receive only its
proxy credential, never its administrative UI token. Request input MUST NOT
select an upstream origin.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] ziggy-authority-boundary
Ziggy MUST obtain current Marshall authority before provider effects and MUST
stop streaming when request authority expires. Guest headers cannot confer VM
identity. Ziggy MUST NOT directly access Marshall's database or repeat inference
on recovery. A persisted admission is not evidence of provider completion.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] ziggy-accounting-unknown
Absent provider usage MUST remain unknown, never zero. Durable events MUST have
stable IDs; retransmission MUST NOT duplicate counted usage. Full spool or failed
admission persistence MUST prevent new provider effects.
